### Pull request previews

Previews run on a separate Cloudflare Worker, `{{ slug | replace('.', '-') | replace('_', '-') }}-preview`, configured in
[`{{ d }}wrangler.preview.jsonc`]({{ blob }}{{ d }}wrangler.preview.jsonc). The `preview` job in `ts.yml` uploads each pull
request's build to it at a `pr-<number>` address, shown in the job summary. Previews are public and
send `X-Robots-Tag: noindex`. A preview is live only while its pull request is open and not a draft:
the job skips drafts and checks the pull request again just before uploading. `preview-retire.yml`
points the address at a "preview closed" page when the pull request closes or turns draft, then
fetches the address and fails unless the page is served. A daily run does the same for pull requests
closed in the last 14 days and for open drafts, in case an event was missed. One-time setup:

1. Run `just repo-settings` to create the `preview` environment, or create it under Settings > Environments.
2. Add the secrets `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` (a token with Workers Scripts: Edit) and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` to that environment.
3. In the Pages project, set Settings > Builds > Branch control > Preview branch to None.

Without the token, the job skips with a notice.
